#: src/AbilitiesService.php:39
msgid "Ask me to find saved recipes by title, ingredient, category, or tag."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:40
msgid "Ask me to import a recipe from a URL, create a recipe variation, or help plan meals for the week."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:41
msgid "Ask me to review and tidy Cook App ingredients, categories, cuisines, or tags."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:67
msgid "When presenting Cook App recipes, include the recipe title and link it with view_url when present."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:71
msgid "When presenting Cook App search results, show concise recipe matches and link each recipe with view_url when present. If no recipes match, say that no Cook App recipe was found instead of guessing from the database."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:75
msgid "When presenting Cook App week plans, summarize planned meals by day and meal slot. Link planned recipes with their view_url when present, and link to the planner using the returned url."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:93
msgid "Abilities for working with Cook App recipes and week plans."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:109
msgid "Search Cook App Recipes"
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:110
msgid "Searches Cook App recipes and returns matching recipe summaries."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:118
msgid "Use this when the user asks to find, list, filter, or choose Cook App recipes. Call without input to list the latest 10 recipes. Return recipe IDs for follow-up get-recipe calls, and use view_url when linking results to the user."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:131
msgid "Get Cook App Recipe"
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:132
msgid "Returns one structured Cook App recipe by ID."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:140
msgid "Recipe post ID."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:150
msgid "Use this when the user asks about one known Cook App recipe. The response includes view_url for linking, flat compatibility ingredients/instructions, named parts for ingredient or instruction sections, notes, taxonomy terms, and variation family data."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:163
msgid "Save Cook App Recipe"
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:164
msgid "Creates a structured Cook App recipe, or updates an existing recipe when an ID is provided."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:172
msgid "Use this when the user asks to save, create, or update a structured Cook App recipe. Pass parts to preserve named ingredient or instruction sections; flat ingredients and instructions remain supported for unsectioned recipes. To add or replace a recipe photo, pass the existing recipe id with image_url. Prefer create-recipe-variation when adapting an existing recipe into a new variation. Link the result using view_url."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:185
msgid "Import Cook App Recipe"
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:186
msgid "Imports a recipe from source_url or pasted recipe text and publishes it."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:193
msgid "Recipe page URL to parse."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:197
msgid "Plain recipe text to parse if no URL can be parsed."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:201
#: src/AbilitiesService.php:656
msgid "Optional image URL to sideload as the recipe photo."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:211
msgid "Use this when the user provides a recipe URL, pasted recipe text, or an image URL to import into Cook App. This publishes the recipe; link the result using view_url."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:224
msgid "Create Cook App Recipe Variation"
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:225
msgid "Creates a child recipe variation from an existing Cook App recipe, copying omitted fields from the source."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:233
msgid "Use this when the user asks for an adapted version of an existing recipe, such as substituting an ingredient they do not have. First call get-recipe for the source, then pass the complete revised recipe fields here so omitted fields intentionally copy from the source. If the source has named parts, pass revised parts to preserve ingredient subsection headers. Link the created variation using view_url."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:246
msgid "Get Cook App Week Plan"
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:247
msgid "Returns the signed-in user's week planner for a normalized week."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:255
msgid "Use this when the user asks what meals are planned for a week. The week_start input can be any date in the week; use the returned url to link to the planner."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:268
msgid "Save Cook App Week Plan"
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:269
msgid "Saves recipe IDs into the signed-in user's week planner meal slots."
msgstr ""

#: src/AbilitiesService.php:277
msgid "Use this when the user asks to add, move, clear, or replace recipes in their week planner. This can clear slots with recipe ID 0 or replace the whole week when replace is true, so confirm ambiguous planner edits before executing."
msgstr ""

